Input: {"question": "Which country is Folia Orientalia from?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 0, "end": 16, "text": "Folia Orientalia"}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 18, "end": 136, "text": "Folia Orientalia is a peer-reviewed academic journal that specializes in the study of Oriental languages and cultures."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 137, "end": 276, "text": "Despite its widespread recognition and influence in the field, the journal's country of origin has been a subject of debate among scholars."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 277, "end": 389, "text": "However, recent studies and evidence have conclusively established that Folia Orientalia hails from Switzerland."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 390, "end": 408, "text": "Early Speculations"}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 410, "end": 546, "text": "The earliest recorded speculation about Folia Orientalia's country of origin dates back to the 1960s, when linguist and Orientalist, Dr."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 547, "end": 679, "text": "Helmut Ritter, suggested that the journal might have originated from a European country with a strong tradition of Oriental studies."}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 680, "end": 886, "text": "[1] Ritter's hypothesis was based on the journal's focus on languages such as Arabic, Persian, and Turkish, which were commonly studied in European academic circles during the 19th and early 20th centuries."}, "D1S9": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 887, "end": 907, "text": "The Swiss Connection"}, "D1S10": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 909, "end": 955, "text": "In the 1990s, a team of researchers led by Dr."}, "D1S11": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 956, "end": 1070, "text": "Ursula Keller, a Swiss historian, conducted an exhaustive study on the history of Oriental studies in Switzerland."}, "D1S12": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1071, "end": 1249, "text": "[2] The study revealed that Switzerland had a thriving community of Orientalists during the 19th and early 20th centuries, with many prominent scholars contributing to the field."}, "D1S13": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1250, "end": 1459, "text": "Keller's team discovered that several Swiss scholars had been involved in the founding and editing of Folia Orientalia, leading them to conclude that the journal was likely to have originated from Switzerland."}, "D1S14": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1460, "end": 1477, "text": "Archival Evidence"}, "D1S15": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1479, "end": 1643, "text": "In 2010, a cache of archival documents was discovered in the University of Zurich's library, which provided conclusive evidence of Folia Orientalia's Swiss origins."}, "D1S16": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1644, "end": 1867, "text": "[3] The documents, which included correspondence between the journal's founders and Swiss academics, revealed that the journal was established in 1920 by a group of Swiss scholars who were passionate about Oriental studies."}, "D1S17": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1868, "end": 2045, "text": "The documents also showed that the journal was initially published by a Swiss publishing house, which further solidified the connection between Folia Orientalia and Switzerland."}, "D1S18": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2046, "end": 2056, "text": "References"}, "D1S19": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2058, "end": 2072, "text": "[1] Ritter, H."}, "D1S20": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2073, "end": 2080, "text": "(1965)."}, "D1S21": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2081, "end": 2136, "text": "\"The Origins of Folia Orientalia: A Speculative Study.\""}, "D1S22": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2137, "end": 2178, "text": "Journal of Oriental Studies, 5(1), 12-25."}, "D1S23": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2179, "end": 2201, "text": "[2] Keller, U., et al."}, "D1S24": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2202, "end": 2209, "text": "(1995)."}, "D1S25": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2210, "end": 2265, "text": "\"Oriental Studies in Switzerland: A Historical Survey.\""}, "D1S26": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2266, "end": 2307, "text": "Swiss Journal of History, 45(2), 123-145."}, "D1S27": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2308, "end": 2350, "text": "[3] University of Zurich Library Archives."}, "D1S28": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2351, "end": 2358, "text": "(2010)."}, "D1S29": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2359, "end": 2397, "text": "\"Folia Orientalia Founding Documents.\""}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 0, "end": 101, "text": "**HEADLINE:** Renowned Academic Journal Folia Orientalia Hails from Poland, a Hub of Oriental Studies"}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 103, "end": 311, "text": "**WARSAW, POLAND** - In the realm of academic publishing, few journals have made a mark as significant as Folia Orientalia, a prestigious publication dedicated to the study of Oriental languages and cultures."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 312, "end": 459, "text": "And, as our investigation reveals, this esteemed journal has its roots firmly planted in Poland, a country with a rich history of Oriental studies."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 460, "end": 591, "text": "Founded in 1954, Folia Orientalia has been a beacon of scholarship, attracting top researchers and academics from around the world."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 592, "end": 818, "text": "The journal's focus on languages such as Arabic, Persian, Turkish, and Mongolian, as well as its exploration of the cultural heritage of the Middle East and Asia, has earned it a reputation as a leading authority in the field."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 819, "end": 835, "text": "According to Dr."}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 836, "end": 1004, "text": "Anna Krasnowolska, a renowned Orientalist and Professor at the University of Warsaw, \"Folia Orientalia has been a cornerstone of Oriental studies in Poland for decades."}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1005, "end": 1134, "text": "Its contributions to the field have been invaluable, and its presence has helped establish Poland as a hub of Oriental research.\""}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1135, "end": 1199, "text": "Data from the journal's publication history supports this claim."}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1200, "end": 1334, "text": "Since its inception, Folia Orientalia has published over 50 volumes, featuring articles from esteemed scholars from Poland and beyond."}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1335, "end": 1491, "text": "The journal's editorial board, comprising leading experts in the field, is based in Poland, further solidifying the country's connection to the publication."}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1492, "end": 1669, "text": "Poland's strong tradition of Oriental studies can be traced back to the 16th century, when the country was a major center of trade and cultural exchange between Europe and Asia."}, "D2S13": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1670, "end": 1844, "text": "This legacy has continued to the present day, with Polish universities and research institutions boasting some of the world's top programs in Oriental languages and cultures."}, "D2S14": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1845, "end": 1940, "text": "\"Folia Orientalia is a testament to Poland's enduring commitment to Oriental studies,\" said Dr."}, "D2S15": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1941, "end": 2033, "text": "Marek Stachowski, Director of the Institute of Oriental Studies at the University of Warsaw."}, "D2S16": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2034, "end": 2172, "text": "\"The journal's presence has not only enriched our academic community but has also helped foster international collaboration and exchange.\""}, "D2S17": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2173, "end": 2281, "text": "In conclusion, the evidence overwhelmingly supports the claim that Folia Orientalia is, indeed, from Poland."}, "D2S18": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2282, "end": 2500, "text": "With its rich history, esteemed editorial board, and contributions to the field of Oriental studies, this journal is a source of pride for Poland and a testament to the country's status as a hub of academic excellence."}}, "original_cards": [], "current_answers": ["Switzerland", "Poland"], "candidate_answers": [{"candidate_id": "R0", "answer": "Switzerland", "origin": "initial"}, {"candidate_id": "R1", "answer": "Poland", "origin": "initial"}]}

